## Summary

**Worktree:** `feat/genesis-git-migration` — commits `13c37b2` (RED) → `63684a3` (GREEN)

### RED — characterization tests (`13c37b2`)
9 tests in `pretender/src/git.rs` pinning current semantics, pass-to-pass:
- staged-only set excludes unstaged worktree changes and untracked files
- staged deletions excluded (even though the file lingers on disk untracked)
- staged rename reports new path only
- unborn-HEAD repo: staged files still returned (empty-tree diff fallback)
- non-repo cwd → typed error
- diff-base set excludes deletions and untracked; bad base ref / unborn HEAD → typed error

Two fixture iterations were needed (a mid-test commit swept up staged changes, and a "staged-then-modified" file is by definition staged) — implementation behavior was correct both times.

### GREEN — migration (`63684a3`)
- `pretender/src/git.rs`: reimplemented on `genesis::git` — `repo_root_from` for root discovery, canonical `run` with explicit root + `EnvPolicy::StripHookContext`
  - `staged_files`: `git diff -z --name-only --cached --diff-filter=AMRCT HEAD`, with 128/unborn-HEAD fallback to the HEAD-less invocation (index vs empty tree — exact git2 `head_tree() == None` parity)
  - `diff_base_files`: `git diff -z --name-only --diff-filter=AMRCT <base> HEAD`
  - `-z` output gives unquoted, NUL-separated paths; canonicalize-with-fallback preserved
- `pretender/Cargo.toml`: **git2 removed**, `genesis-vibes` bumped `"0.12.3"` → `"0.13"` (resolves to 0.13.0)
- `pretender/src/main.rs`: `gitignore_walk` fixture now uses plain `git init` subprocess

Gotcha worth noting: the genesis-vibes crate renames its lib (`[lib] name = "genesis"`), so the import is `use genesis::git::...`, not `genesis_vibes::...`.

